    <sys:String x:Key="Gaming.ClickThrough">Click-through</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Gaming.ClickThroughTip">Mouse clicks pass through the overlay to the window underneath. Turn off here (or press Ctrl+Shift+F9) to move or resize it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Gaming.Visible">Visible</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Gaming.EmptyTitle">No active overlays</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Gaming.EmptyText">Choose a window in Sources and select Create overlay. The overlay appears on top of everything and mirrors the window live.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Gaming.BrowseSources">Browse sources</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Gaming.GoodToKnow">GOOD TO KNOW</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Gaming.TipGamesTitle">Windowed &amp; borderless games</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Gaming.TipGamesText">Overlays appear above windowed and borderless-fullscreen games (e.g. Euro Truck Simulator 2 in borderless mode). Exclusive fullscreen draws above all windows, so overlays can't show there. VIZEN never touches the game process.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Gaming.TipMoveTitle">Move, resize, snap</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Gaming.TipMoveText">Drag to move, drag edges to resize, double-click to remove letterboxing. Ctrl+Shift+F9 toggles click-through, Ctrl+Shift+F10 shows/hides all.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Gaming.TipMinimizedTitle">Minimized sources pause</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Gaming.TipMinimizedText">Windows stops rendering minimized windows, so the overlay freezes until the source is restored. Windows covered by other windows keep updating (verified with Chrome/Edge too). With “Keep source active”, VIZEN automatically brings a minimized source back behind the active window.</sys:String>
