    <sys:String x:Key="Perf.Col.Pipeline">Pipeline</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Perf.HealthNote">SOURCE LIMITED appears only when VIZEN's capture thread is mostly idle, which means the low frame rate really comes from the captured app. CAPTURE / PROCESSING LIMITED: VIZEN cannot take frames from Windows fast enough. RENDER / PRESENTATION LIMITED: frames arrive but are not displayed in time. UNKNOWN: frames are being lost, but the measurements do not point to a single cause.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Perf.Test">Performance tests (no game needed)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Perf.TestPattern">Test-pattern window</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Perf.TestPatternDescription">Opens a 1920×1080 window, in a separate process, that changes at exactly 30 or 60 fps and shows a frame-number marker. Select it in Sources (VIZEN Test Pattern) and create overlays: this measures real Windows capture, and "Frames lost end to end" counts every skipped or repeated frame precisely.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Perf.Synthetic">Synthetic source</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Perf.SyntheticDescription">Opens an overlay whose frames are generated by VIZEN itself (1920×1080). It tests only VIZEN's processing and display, not Windows capture, so a good result here does not prove that real capture is perfect.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Perf.Open30">30 fps</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Perf.Open60">60 fps</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Perf.Export">Export diagnostics</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Perf.ExportDescription">Saves this PC's details and the last five minutes of measurements for every capture to a JSON file in Documents\VIZEN Diagnostics. Nothing is sent anywhere.</sys:String>
