    <sys:String x:Key="Draw.HowToTitle">How to</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Draw.HowTo">Turn Smart Draw on and start drawing: pick a tool on the toolbar (at the top of the screen; drag its left edge to move it). Rectangle and ellipse: hold Shift for a square or a circle. Text: click where you want it, type, and press Enter to finish (Shift+Enter starts a new line); click an existing text with the Text tool to edit it. Eraser: Precision (default) cuts freehand lines where its circle passes and removes shapes and text whole; Object removes everything it touches whole; size 5–100. Esc leaves draw mode; Ctrl+Z and Ctrl+Y undo and redo while drawing.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Draw.HotkeyHint">Global shortcuts (you can change them in Settings → Hotkeys): Ctrl+Shift+F7 turns Smart Draw on or off · Ctrl+Shift+F6 switches between draw mode and pass-through · Ctrl+Shift+F5 shows or hides the drawings · Ctrl+Shift+F4 clears everything (press twice to confirm).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Draw.Limits">Limitations: you cannot draw over games running in exclusive fullscreen (use Fullscreen Windowed or Borderless instead). The taskbar area always stays free, so you can reach Windows at any time. Smart Draw only places a window over your screen; it never interacts with your game.</sys:String>
