    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.Eyebrow">03 — SMART AUDIO FOCUS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.Title">Smart Audio Focus</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.Description">When someone talks on Discord, your music and game get quieter by themselves. When it is quiet again, they come back. Your own volumes are kept.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.PriorityLabel">Which app must be heard clearly?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.PriorityHint">Usually your chat app, for example Discord. If it is missing, open it and let it make a sound.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.NoApps">No app is making sound right now. Open Discord (or the app you want), then come back.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.DuckLabel">What should get quieter?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.AllOthers">All other apps</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.TuneLabel">How it works</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.Duck">How much quieter</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.DuckValue">At {1} % of their volume</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.DuckTip">How quiet the other apps get while the priority app is heard.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.Sensitivity">When it starts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.SensitivityTip">Move right if it does not react when your friend talks; move left if it reacts to small noises.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.Level">Priority app level</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.LevelTip">The priority app's sound right now. The marker is the sensitivity: above it, the other apps get quieter.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.Attack">Going quiet</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.AttackTip">Time for the others to get quieter once the priority app is heard.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.Hold">Waits</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.HoldTip">How long the others stay quieter after it went silent.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.Release">Comes back in</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.ReleaseTip">Time for the others to return to their volume.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.Restore">Restore volumes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.RestoreTip">Brings every app back to its own volume now.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Focus.Note">Audio Focus listens to how loud the sound is, not to words, so a notification sound can also lower the others for a moment. If Discord's own &quot;attenuation&quot; option is on, keep only one of the two on.</sys:String>
